FILE: app/src/skip-ahead.ts
```ts
import { updateAnimationManager } from "@babylonjs/lite";
import type { AnimationManager } from "@babylonjs/lite";

export function skipAhead(manager: AnimationManager, ms: number): void {
    const saved = manager.fixedDeltaMs;
    manager.fixedDeltaMs = 0;
    try {
        updateAnimationManager(manager, ms);
    } finally {
        manager.fixedDeltaMs = saved;
    }
}
```

I added `src/skip-ahead.ts` which temporarily zeroes `fixedDeltaMs` so that `updateAnimationManager` uses the exact `ms` you pass (per note 21, a positive `fixedDeltaMs` would override it), then restores it in a `finally` so the manager's stepping behaviour is unchanged on later frames. I'm not sure of anything; the one assumption is that `updateAnimationManager` works even when the manager isn't in its RAF loop (i.e. `running` is false), which matches your description of stepping it yourself each frame.
